# Slice 346 (the book, forms-declare-or-call): a form on a path head. Box\hits (here main\data\Box\hits) is a known
# place of an int, so `main\data\Box\hits: 1` is refused (8); the value is written by `main\data\Box\hits := 1`.
# Plan M11 5v: the declarations of ordinary Structures live in the data part of main; the root holds places and reads
# the Structures by paths through main\data. main has no code, so there is no call: its part code is the empty `()`.
sub: main () (
    Box:
        int: hits 0
) ()
main\data\Box\hits: 1
int: after main\data\Box\hits
